/-! # Extending local finite presentation from a schematically dense open

Source: Stacks Project, More on Morphisms of Spaces, Tag 0877,
`lemma-flat-finite-type-finitely-presented-over-dense-open-X`
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-flat-finite-presentation-dense-open).

Quasi-compactness is tested on affine étale charts. Schematic density is sectionwise
injectivity of the structure-sheaf map: two regular functions agree if their restrictions
to every étale chart of the inverse image agree. The restricted morphism is the second
projection of the canonical sheaf pullback, bundled using the existing closure theorem.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace

/-- A flat locally finite type map is locally finitely presented if this holds over a
quasi-compact schematically dense open subspace. No separatedness or quasi-compactness
of the map itself is required.

Source: Stacks Project, More on Morphisms of Spaces, Tag 0877,
`lemma-flat-finite-type-finitely-presented-over-dense-open-X`, via Tags 0876 and 081P
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-flat-finite-presentation-dense-open).

Proof:
1. Test on compatible étale scheme charts U → X and T → Y. The resulting U → T is
flat and locally of finite type by def-sfb-space-morphism-properties. The inverse image
W of V is retrocompact: its intersections with affine opens of T are quasi-compact by
the hypothesis on j. Schematic density restricts to T by evaluating the assumed
sectionwise injection on its étale charts. The restriction over W is locally finitely
presented by the base-change chart test (lem-trf-space-fibre-products-etale-covers and
lem-weil-pbc-etale-composition-cancellation).
2. Restrict to affine pieces Spec B → Spec A, and choose a polynomial surjection
P = A[t₁,…,tₙ] → B using def-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra. On H = Spec P the associated
module F of B is quasi-coherent of finite type, since it is cyclic over P. The polynomial
map H → Spec A is locally finitely presented. Use pqf-lem-associated-sections-localize
and lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-finite-type-affine to identify its sections and finiteness.
3. Flatness of Spec B → Spec A makes B flat over A by
lem-weil-pbc-flat-morphism-affine-criterion. The affine-chart relative-flatness criterion
(lem-pc-affine-chart-relative-flat-criterion) makes F flat over Spec A in the sense of
def-pc-scheme-module-flat-over, including the zero stalks outside its support.
4. On each principal open D(a) contained in W, B_a is finitely presented over A_a by
lem-weil-pbc-lfp-affine-opens-finite-presentation. The kernel of P_a → B_a is finitely
generated by lem-weil-pbc-finite-presentation-surjection-kernel-fg. Its generators give
a finite module presentation of B_a over P_a (def-sc-finitely-presented-module).
The associated-sections formula and affine sheaf criterion give finite presentation
of F over the inverse image of W.
5. Apply lem-trf-flat-finite-type-dense-presentation to H → Spec A and F, using the
retrocompact schematically dense W. Thus F is finitely presented everywhere. The affine
criterion gives a finitely presented P-module B.
6. The surjective-module kernel theorem
(lem-trf-finite-presentation-surjective-module-kernel) makes ker(P → B) finitely generated.
This is a finite algebra presentation (def-weil-pbc-finitely-presented-algebra), so
Spec B → Spec A is locally finitely presented (def-sbc-locally-finite-presentation).
The affine pieces cover the chart, and arbitrary compatible charts give the conclusion
by def-sfb-space-morphism-properties. Only affine pieces were used. -/
theorem locallyOfFinitePresentation_of_flat_of_denseOpen
    {S : Scheme.{u}} {X Y V : AlgebraicSpace S} (f : X ⟶ Y) (j : V ⟶ Y)
    (hflat : MapIsFlat f) (hft : MapIsLocally (@LocallyOfFiniteType) f)
    (hj : IsRepresentableWith (fun _ _ p ↦ IsOpenImmersion p.left) j.hom.hom)
    (hqc : ∀ T : Y.EtaleSite, IsAffine T.obj.left.left →
      ∃ (U : Over S) (p : U ⟶ T.obj.left) (q : yoneda.obj U ⟶ V.obj.obj),
        IsPullback q (yoneda.map p) j.hom.hom T.obj.hom ∧ QuasiCompact p.left)
    (hdense : ∀ (T : Y.EtaleSite) (a b : Y.structureSheaf.obj.obj (op T)),
      (∀ (U : V.EtaleSite) (p : U.obj.left ⟶ T.obj.left),
        U.obj.hom ≫ j.hom.hom = yoneda.map p ≫ T.obj.hom →
        (Scheme.Γ.map p.left.op).hom a = (Scheme.Γ.map p.left.op).hom b) → a = b)
    (hfp : MapIsLocallyOfFinitePresentation
      (ObjectProperty.homMk (Limits.pullback.snd f.hom j.hom) :
        ⟨Limits.pullback f.hom j.hom, (fibreProduct_isAlgebraicSpace X V Y f j).1⟩ ⟶ V)) :
    MapIsLocallyOfFinitePresentation f := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace
